# Vendored chart dependencies. Regenerated by `helm dependency build`.
# Chart.lock IS committed ... a lockfile you do not commit is not a lockfile,
# and without it a fresh clone cannot render.
charts/*/charts/
*.tgz

# `helm dependency update` unpacks into charts/<layer>/tmpcharts-<pid>/ and
# leaves the directory behind when it is interrupted. 71 of them had
# accumulated by 2026-08-30, none ignored, all of them one `git add -A` away
# from the product tree. They are byte-for-byte copies of vendored upstream
# charts, which the line above already refuses.
charts/*/tmpcharts-*/

build/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Minted SealedSecrets, if anyone runs tools/mint-secrets.sh from a clone of
# THIS repository. SealedSecrets are safe to commit ... to your own site repo,
# which is the point of them ... but this is not that repo, and `git add -A`
# from here would sweep freshly minted credentials into the product tree.
# The tool now defaults to the directory you run it from, so this is a belt to
# the fix's braces rather than the fix itself. Added 2026-08-25.
secrets/
pub-sealed-secrets.pem
sealed-secrets-key.backup.yaml

# Git plumbing that belongs in .git/ and never at the root. FETCH_HEAD was a
# TRACKED, zero-byte file here until 2026-09-01 (TM-0268) ... a `git fetch` run
# somewhere it should not have been, then swept up by `git add -A`. Nothing
# broke, which is why nothing caught it; an external reviewer found it in about
# four seconds and read every operational claim afterwards one notch more
# sceptically. Ignored as a class, and CI fails on any of them being tracked,
# because gitignore does not affect a file that is already in the index.
/FETCH_HEAD
/ORIG_HEAD
/MERGE_HEAD
/COMMIT_EDITMSG

# Local handoff / apply scripts. Generated per working session, run once, deleted.
# Ignored as a class rather than by prefix so a new script shape never starts life
# unignored. Note that gitignore does not affect already-tracked files.
_*.sh

# tools/render-diff.sh writes its comparison trees here. Untracked scratch, and
# it was NOT ignored until 2026-09-03, which is one `git add -A` away from
# committing a duplicate of the repository into the repository. It had also
# grown 30 levels deep (render-diff/tree-b/render-diff/tree-b/...) because the
# script copied its input into a subdirectory of itself, and 281 MB of that
# turned the local docs-link gate red on 568 links that do not exist.
/render-diff/

# The installer's own inputs and outputs, which docs/deployment/install.md
# Phase 1 tells the reader to create INSIDE their Tockmox clone:
#
#   cp install/tockmox.yaml.example tockmox.yaml
#
# and site.path defaults to ./tockmox-site. Following the page verbatim
# therefore leaves two untracked entries in this repository, and tockmox.yaml
# carries a site's LAN CIDR and internal DNS zone. Ignored so a reader's own
# configuration cannot be committed here by accident.
/tockmox.yaml
/tockmox-site/

# Python bytecode from the executed-docs harness. `tests/executed-docs/lib/`
# is imported on every run, so a `.pyc` appears and sits in `git status`
# forever ... on a repo whose release procedure READS `git status`. It is one
# line against a reader learning to skim that surface, which is the actual
# cost (TM-0677). Checked when this was added: no `.pyc` was already tracked,
# and an ignore rule would not have untracked one if it were.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The rendered documentation site. tools/build-docs.sh writes it to build/docs-site
# by default (covered by build/ above) for tools/publish-docs.sh to upload, and
# it is never committed: it is 7 MB of generated HTML and a committed copy would
# go stale on the next docs edit.
